{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"f094b4c4956f4ead41f798d9b7b71c875be78a84ed6a4faa9c25ff978b95e820","digest":{"component_or_area":"snapshot delta tree","key_entities":["src/rebar/_snapshot/delta_tree.py","_apply_delta","checkout-index","read-tree","git_run","run_git","_GIT_TIMEOUT","src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py","subprocess.TimeoutExpired"],"problem_keywords":["timeout","unbounded subprocess","git checkout-index","delta tree","snapshot"],"propositions":["The checkout-index subprocess call in _apply_delta lacks a timeout parameter while its sibling read-tree call is bounded by _GIT_TIMEOUT (300s)","checkout-index is the expensive filesystem-intensive operation in _apply_delta and is most likely to stall on slow or wedged volumes, yet has no upper bound or diagnostic for distinguishing hung state from slow progress","The asymmetry exists within a single function operating on the same index in the same failure domain with no stated intent to leave checkout-index unbounded","A timeout in checkout-index should be caught and return False from _apply_delta so callers fall back to full materialization rather than raising an unhandled exception"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787648748018731001,"uuid":"c650a1de-9ca0-476e-8b2b-f13a308743e3"}